#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:3
msgid "/proc/sys/crypto/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:5
msgid ""
"These files show up in ``/proc/sys/crypto/``, depending on the kernel "
"configuration:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:13
msgid "af_alg_restrict"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:15
msgid "Controls the level of restriction of AF_ALG."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:17
msgid ""
"AF_ALG is a deprecated and rarely-used userspace interface that is a "
"frequent source of vulnerabilities. It also unnecessarily exposes a large "
"number of kernel implementation details. For more information about AF_ALG, "
"see :ref:`Documentation/crypto/userspace-if.rst "
"<crypto_userspace_interface>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:23
msgid ""
"Starting in Linux v7.3, AF_ALG supports only a limited set of algorithms by "
"default. This sysctl allows the system administrator to remove this "
"restriction when needed for compatibility reasons, or to go further and "
"disable AF_ALG entirely. The default value is 1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:29
msgid "0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:29
msgid "AF_ALG is unrestricted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:31
msgid "1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:31
msgid ""
"AF_ALG is supported with a limited list of algorithms. The list is designed "
"for compatibility with known users such as iwd and bluez that haven't yet "
"been fixed to use userspace crypto code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:35
msgid ""
"Specifically, there is an allowlist for unprivileged processes and a "
"somewhat longer allowlist for processes that hold CAP_SYS_ADMIN or "
"CAP_NET_ADMIN in the initial user namespace."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:39
msgid ""
"Attempts to bind() an AF_ALG socket with a disallowed algorithm fail with "
"ENOENT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:42
msgid "2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:42
msgid ""
"AF_ALG is completely disabled. Attempts to create an AF_ALG socket fail with "
"EAFNOSUPPORT."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:47
msgid "fips_enabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:49
msgid "Read-only flag that indicates whether FIPS mode is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:51
msgid "``0``: FIPS mode is disabled (default)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:52
msgid "``1``: FIPS mode is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:54
msgid ""
"This value is set at boot time via the ``fips=1`` kernel command line "
"parameter. When enabled, the cryptographic API will restrict the use of "
"certain algorithms and perform self-tests to ensure compliance with FIPS "
"(Federal Information Processing Standards) requirements, such as FIPS 140-2 "
"and the newer FIPS 140-3, depending on the kernel configuration and the "
"module in use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:62
msgid "fips_name"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:64
msgid ""
"Read-only file that contains the name of the FIPS module currently in use. "
"The value is typically configured via the ``CONFIG_CRYPTO_FIPS_NAME`` kernel "
"configuration option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:69
msgid "fips_version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../admin-guide/sysctl/crypto.rst:71
msgid ""
"Read-only file that contains the version string of the FIPS module. If "
"``CONFIG_CRYPTO_FIPS_CUSTOM_VERSION`` is set, it uses the value from "
"``CONFIG_CRYPTO_FIPS_VERSION``. Otherwise, it defaults to the kernel release "
"version (``UTS_RELEASE``)."
msgstr ""

